{"tool_name":"wgd","contents":["bioconda","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"wgd","version":"2.0.38","home":"https://github.com/heche-psb/wgd","documentation":"https://wgdv2.readthedocs.io/en/latest/","license":"GPL-3.0-or-later","summary":"wgd v2: a suite of tools to uncover and date ancient polyploidy and whole-genome duplication","identifiers":["biotools:wgd","doi:10.1007/978-1-0716-2561-3_1","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btae272"],"license_file":"LICENSE","build":{"entry_points":["wgd=cli:cli"],"noarch":"python","number":0,"run_exports":[null],"script":" -m pip install . --no-deps --no-build-isolation --no-cache-dir -vvv"},"requirements":{"host":["pip","python >=3.6,<3.10"],"run":["python >=3.6,<3.10","mafft","paml","diamond","mcl"]},"source_url":"https://pypi.io/packages/source/w/wgd/wgd-2.0.38.tar.gz","test":{"imports":["wgd"]}},"biotools":{"id":"wgd","home":"https://github.com/arzwa/wgd","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"wgd-simple command line tools for the analysis of ancient whole-genome duplications.\n\nCopyright (C) 2018 Arthur Zwaenepoel.\n\nVIB/UGent center for plant systems biology - Bioinformatics & evolutionary genomics group http://bioinformatics.psb.ugent.be/beg/.\n\nwgd - simple command line tools for the analysis of ancient whole-genome duplications.\n\nPython package and command line interface (CLI) for the analysis of whole-genome duplications (WGDs). Tested with Python3 on Linux. If you don't have python or pip installed a simple sudo apt-get install python3-pip should do.","addition_date":"2020-09-03T19:16:24Z","last_update_date":"2020-09-08T14:28:48Z","version":["1.1.1"],"collections":["BIG N2N","UGent","VIB"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:wgd","credit":[{"email":"yves.vandepeer@psb.vib-ugent.be","name":"Yves Van de Peer","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4327-3730","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"}]}],"name":"wgd","owner":"bits@vib.be","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOINFORMATICS/BTY915","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author(s) 2018.Ancient whole-genome duplications (WGDs) have been uncovered in almost all major lineages of life on Earth and the search for traces or remnants of such events has become standard practice in most genome analyses. This is especially true for plants, where ancient WGDs are abundant. Common approaches to find evidence for ancient WGDs include the construction of KS distributions and the analysis of intragenomic colinearity. Despite the increased interest in WGDs and the acknowledgment of their evolutionary importance, user-friendly and comprehensive tools for their analysis are lacking. Here, we present an easy to use command-line tool for KS distribution construction named wgd. The wgd suite provides commonly used KS and colinearity analysis workflows together with tools for modeling and visualization, rendering these analyses accessible to genomics researchers in a convenient manner.","authors":[{"name":"Van De Peer Y."},{"name":"Zwaenepoel A."}],"citationCount":32,"date":"2019-06-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Wgd-simple command line tools for the analysis of ancient whole-genome duplications"},"pmcid":"PMC6581438","pmid":"30398564"}],"topic":[{"term":"Genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0622"},{"term":"Plant biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0780"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"wgd","home":"https://bio.tools/wgd","license":"GPL-3.0","version":"1.1.1","summary":"wgd-simple command line tools for the analysis of ancient whole-genome duplications.\n\nCopyright (C) 2018 Arthur Zwaenepoel.\n\nVIB/UGent center for plant systems biology - Bioinformatics & evolutionary genomics group http://bioinformatics.psb.ugent.be/beg/.\n\nwgd - simple command line too